<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Evaluate Exponential Expressions: Mini-Lesson Review</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01223</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Evaluate Exponential Expressions: Mini-Lesson Review</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f76894cb-9b00-4a8b-8629-9981163fa0db</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <note class="mini-lesson-review" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Question #3: Evaluate Exponential Expressions</title>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
        <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_OR_U5_Q3"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
      </note>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Evaluating Exponential Expressions</title>
      <para id="para-00002">A power is repeated multiplication of the same factor. The factor is the
        base, and the number of times the base is used as a factor is the exponent. The expression
        is called a power.</para>
      <para id="para-00003"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mi>B</m:mi>
            <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            <m:mi>s</m:mi>
            <m:mi>e</m:mi>
            <m:mo>→</m:mo>
            <m:msup>
              <m:munder>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mo>⏟</m:mo>
              </m:munder>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>←</m:mo>
                <m:mi>E</m:mi>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:mi>o</m:mi>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mi>e</m:mi>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mi>t</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math></para>
      <para id="para-00004">The expression <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> is read:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>five to the power of three</item>
        <item>five to the third power</item>
        <item>five cubed</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00005"><m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> means 5 is
        used as a factor 3 times: <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:msup>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            <m:mi>·</m:mi>
            <m:mn>5</m:mn>
            <m:mo>=</m:mo>
            <m:mn>125</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00006">Evaluate each expression.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
        <item><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> Use <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> as a
          factor 5 times. <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>32</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
    
    <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>32</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>

        </item>
        <item><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> Use
          order of operations. Evaluate the exponent first.  <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>81</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> Then multiply. <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>81</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>567</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
    
    <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>567</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        </item>
      </list>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.8</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>  Use
          order of operations. Evaluate the exponent first.  <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.8</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.8</m:mn>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mn>0.8</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.64</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> Then multiply. <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.64</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>12.8</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
    
    <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>20</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0.8</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mn>12.8</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        </item>
      </list>
      <note class="try" id="note-00001">
        <title> Try It: Evaluating Exponential Expressions</title>
<exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">

            <para id="para-00007">Evaluate <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.2</m:mn>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
        .</para>

            <para id="para-00008">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
        button to compare your work.</para>

          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer:</para>

            <para id="para-00010">Here is how to evaluate this exponential expression.</para>

            <para id="para-00011"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Use order of operations and evaluate
        the power first. <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.2</m:mn>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.2</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>0.2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.04</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>

            <para id="para-00012"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Next, multiply. <m:math
                display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.04</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
    <m:math
                display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>50</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0.2</m:mn>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></para>

          </solution>
        </exercise></note>

      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
        <title>Check Your Understanding</title>
        <exercise id="a282e7d5-8ff3-48ff-bde9-7d135038dcfe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Evaluate <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  <m:msup>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:msup>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>
              .</para>
            <para id="para-00014">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00015">27</para>
            <para id="para-00016">216</para>
            <para id="para-00017">18</para>
            <para id="para-00018">54</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! Check yourself: Use order of operations and evaluate the
              power first. Then multiply the result by 2.</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Try again. Let’s try again in a different way: Use order of
              operations and evaluate the power first. Then multiply the result by <m:math
                display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>